{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014UjM2UF2m1QLH1d7oqpKXv","type":"tool_result","content":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n11:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n12:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n13:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n14:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n15:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n16:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n53:    mode: null,\n334:      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n526:// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n666:let lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\n670:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n673:  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n680:  AIHub.ready();\n681:  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n682:  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n688:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n693:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n694:  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n716:  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n725:    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n748:  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n757:  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n786:  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n805:      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n811:    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n812:    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n846:  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n848:    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968","uuid":"702409df-958b-4652-93f3-d0e638d3f043","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:24.612Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n11:<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n12:<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n13:<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n14:<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n15:<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n16:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n53:    mode: null,\n334:      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n526:// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n666:let lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\n670:  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n673:  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n680:  AIHub.ready();\n681:  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n682:  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n688:  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n693:  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n694:  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n716:  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n725:    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n748:  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n757:  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n786:  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n805:      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n811:    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n812:    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n846:  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n848:    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014UjM2UF2m1QLH1d7oqpKXv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggygm7hYGF4Zs6vzppJc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ej64h5RaHU6YCybCSZ2tvy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,30p;500,560p;640,870p' examples/arena.html | grep -v \"^\\s*$\" | head -330","description":"Read the arena shared-world example's integration code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4247,"cache_read_input_tokens":187100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4247},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968","uuid":"635b9cc9-7055-4bb5-965d-32a7938703f3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:28.249Z","request_id":"req_011CggygkuJx3bZH4CBStL7b","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Ej64h5RaHU6YCybCSZ2tvy":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/work/_research/hub2/ai-hub/lib/hub && sed -n '1,30p;500,560p;640,870p' examples/arena.html | grep -v \"^\\s*$\" | head -330","description":"Read the arena shared-world example's integration code"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01Ej64h5RaHU6YCybCSZ2tvy":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/work/_research/hub2/ai-hub/lib/hub"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ej64h5RaHU6YCybCSZ2tvy","type":"tool_result","content":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  };\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\n    if (!hub.active) return;\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\n  };\n  root.AIHub = hub;\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<canvas id=\"c\" aria-label=\"Star Arena\"></canvas>\n<script>\n'use strict';\n// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n//   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n//   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n//   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n//   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n// First to TARGET stars wins.\nconst W = 800, H = 600, R = 18, SPEED = 260, TARGET = 10;\nconst canvas = document.getElementById('c');\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet pointer = null;\nlet audio = null;\naddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) return menuKey(e.key);\n  keys.add(e.key.toLowerCase());\n  gesture();\n});\naddEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys.delete(e.key.toLowerCase()));\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { pointer = e; gesture(); });\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (pointer) pointer = e; });\naddEventListener('pointerup', () => { pointer = null; });\nfunction beep(freq) {\n  if (!audio || muted) return;\n  const o = audio.createOscillator(), g = audio.createGain();\n  o.frequency.value = freq; g.gain.value = 0.05;\n  o.connect(g).connect(audio.destination);\n  o.start(); o.stop(audio.currentTime + 0.08);\n}\n// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\nconst PAD = { cross: 0, circle: 1, triangle: 3, create: 8, options: 9, up: 12, down: 13 };\nlet pad = null, padNow = [], padWas = [];\nfunction readPad() {\n}\nfunction newStar() {\n  game.star = { x: 40 + game.rng() * (W - 80), y: 40 + game.rng() * (H - 80), n: game.star.n + 1 };\n}\n/** Your own player, from your own stick. Every copy moves its own, every frame, host or not. */\nfunction move(p, s, dt) {\n  const speed = SPEED * (s.sprint ? 1.5 : 1);\n  p.x = Math.max(R, Math.min(W - R, p.x + s.x * speed * dt));\n  p.y = Math.max(R, Math.min(H - R, p.y + s.y * speed * dt));\n}\nconst touching = (p) => Math.hypot(p.x - game.star.x, p.y - game.star.y) < R + 12;\n// ---- solo: the game as it plays on its own\nfunction solo() {\n  game.players = [{ id: 0, name: 'You', color: '#f5b700', x: W / 2, y: H / 2, score: 0 }];\n  game.phase = 'title';\n  game.message = 'Star Arena — press any key or tap to play';\n}\nlet soloEnds = 0;\n// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n// is drawn where you put it.\nlet hub = null;\nlet lastSent = 0;\nlet lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\nlet claimed = -1;            // the star this copy claimed last: one claim a star\nasync function connect() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n  if (!info) return solo();\n  hub = info;\n  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n  game.players = info.players.map((p) => ({ ...p, x: 0, y: 0, score: 0, gone: false, at: -Infinity }));\n  place(game.players);\n  newStar();                 // the first star comes from the seed: the same on every copy\n  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n  game.phase = 'waiting';\n  game.message = 'Get ready…';\n  AIHub.ready();\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'me') heard(from, data);\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'claim') take(from, data.n);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 's') applySnapshot(data);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 'pick' && data.id !== hub.me) beep(330);   // your own cheered at the claim\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  if (!audio) {\n    try { audio = new AudioContext(); } catch { audio = null; }\n  }\n  audio?.resume?.().catch(() => {});\n}\nfunction gesture() {\n  unlockAudio();\n  if (!hub && (game.phase === 'title' || game.phase === 'over')) {\n    solo();\n    game.phase = 'playing';\n    soloEnds = performance.now() + 60_000;\n  }\n}\n// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\nlet last = performance.now();\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffd34d';\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(game.star.x, game.star.y, 10 + Math.sin(now / 150) * 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n  }\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  for (const p of game.players) {\n    if (p.gone) continue;\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = '14px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(`${p.name} ${p.score}`, p.x, p.y - R - 8);\n  }\n  ctx.font = '22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n    ctx.font = 'bold 96px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);\n  } else if (game.phase !== 'playing') {\n    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,.55)'; ctx.fillRect(0, H / 2 - 120, W, 240);\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(game.message, W / 2, H / 2 - 70);\n    const rows = game.standings\n      ? game.standings.flatMap((ids, place) => ids.map((id) => [place + 1, game.players.find((p) => p.id === id)]))\n      : game.players.map((p) => [null, p]);\n    ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n    rows.slice(0, 4).forEach(([place, p], i) => {\n      if (!p) return;\n      ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n      ctx.fillText(`${place ? place + '. ' : ''}${p.name}${hub && p.id === hub.me ? ' (you)' : ''} — ${p.score}`, W / 2, H / 2 - 30 + i * 28);\n    });\n  }\n  if (menu.open) drawMenu();\n}\nfunction drawMenu() {\n  ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(10,8,20,.82)'; ctx.fillRect(W / 2 - 170, 150, 340, 70 + menu.items.length * 40);\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = 'bold 22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillText('Settings', W / 2, 186);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968","uuid":"36bc2b41-c456-47d1-9fd8-193e9b012975","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:28.303Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  };\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\n    if (!hub.active) return;\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\n  };\n  root.AIHub = hub;\n})(typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis);\n</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<canvas id=\"c\" aria-label=\"Star Arena\"></canvas>\n<script>\n'use strict';\n// Star Arena: the smallest honest shared-world game, the plain form of \"Shared\n// world\" (lib/hub/README.md): the host runs the world. Every copy moves its own\n// player from its own stick, at once, and never waits for the network to do\n// it. The host's copy runs only what is shared, the star and the scores:\n//   me     each other copy → the host, ~15 a second, unreliable: where my player is\n//   s      the host → everyone, ~15 a second, unreliable: every player, its score, the star\n//   claim  a copy → the host, reliable, once a star: my player touched star n\n//   pick   the host → everyone, reliable: player id took star n\n// The host takes each player where it says it is, and a claim scores unless\n// someone else got there first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends the round.\n// The host may be a server, a copy with no player of its own (AIHub.server):\n// it runs the same host code, moves nobody and draws nothing.\n// First to TARGET stars wins.\nconst W = 800, H = 600, R = 18, SPEED = 260, TARGET = 10;\nconst canvas = document.getElementById('c');\nconst ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\nconst keys = new Set();\nlet pointer = null;\nlet audio = null;\naddEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') return toggleMenu();\n  if (menu.open) return menuKey(e.key);\n  keys.add(e.key.toLowerCase());\n  gesture();\n});\naddEventListener('keyup', (e) => keys.delete(e.key.toLowerCase()));\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { pointer = e; gesture(); });\ncanvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => { if (pointer) pointer = e; });\naddEventListener('pointerup', () => { pointer = null; });\nfunction beep(freq) {\n  if (!audio || muted) return;\n  const o = audio.createOscillator(), g = audio.createGain();\n  o.frequency.value = freq; g.gain.value = 0.05;\n  o.connect(g).connect(audio.destination);\n  o.start(); o.stop(audio.currentTime + 0.08);\n}\n// ---- the controller, in the browser's standard mapping (a PS5 DualSense:\n// Cross 0, Circle 1, Triangle 3, Create 8, Options 9, D-pad 12-15, left stick\n// axes 0 and 1). Buttons count on the frame they go down.\nconst PAD = { cross: 0, circle: 1, triangle: 3, create: 8, options: 9, up: 12, down: 13 };\nlet pad = null, padNow = [], padWas = [];\nfunction readPad() {\n}\nfunction newStar() {\n  game.star = { x: 40 + game.rng() * (W - 80), y: 40 + game.rng() * (H - 80), n: game.star.n + 1 };\n}\n/** Your own player, from your own stick. Every copy moves its own, every frame, host or not. */\nfunction move(p, s, dt) {\n  const speed = SPEED * (s.sprint ? 1.5 : 1);\n  p.x = Math.max(R, Math.min(W - R, p.x + s.x * speed * dt));\n  p.y = Math.max(R, Math.min(H - R, p.y + s.y * speed * dt));\n}\nconst touching = (p) => Math.hypot(p.x - game.star.x, p.y - game.star.y) < R + 12;\n// ---- solo: the game as it plays on its own\nfunction solo() {\n  game.players = [{ id: 0, name: 'You', color: '#f5b700', x: W / 2, y: H / 2, score: 0 }];\n  game.phase = 'title';\n  game.message = 'Star Arena — press any key or tap to play';\n}\nlet soloEnds = 0;\n// ---- hub mode. Every other player also has tx, ty: where it last said it is\n// (and on the host, at: when). It is drawn easing toward there; your own player\n// is drawn where you put it.\nlet hub = null;\nlet lastSent = 0;\nlet lastSnap = -Infinity;    // the newest snapshot taken, by its AIHub.time()\nlet claimed = -1;            // the star this copy claimed last: one claim a star\nasync function connect() {\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4] });\n  if (!info) return solo();\n  hub = info;\n  game.rng = AIHub.rng('stars');\n  game.players = info.players.map((p) => ({ ...p, x: 0, y: 0, score: 0, gone: false, at: -Infinity }));\n  place(game.players);\n  newStar();                 // the first star comes from the seed: the same on every copy\n  // The hub's card collects everyone's ready: ready up as soon as the arena is built.\n  game.phase = 'waiting';\n  game.message = 'Get ready…';\n  AIHub.ready();\n  AIHub.on('start', () => { game.phase = 'playing'; unlockAudio(); });\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'me') heard(from, data);\n    if (hub.isHost && data.t === 'claim') take(from, data.n);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 's') applySnapshot(data);\n    if (from === hub.host && data.t === 'pick' && data.id !== hub.me) beep(330);   // your own cheered at the claim\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  if (!audio) {\n    try { audio = new AudioContext(); } catch { audio = null; }\n  }\n  audio?.resume?.().catch(() => {});\n}\nfunction gesture() {\n  unlockAudio();\n  if (!hub && (game.phase === 'title' || game.phase === 'over')) {\n    solo();\n    game.phase = 'playing';\n    soloEnds = performance.now() + 60_000;\n  }\n}\n// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\nlet last = performance.now();\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffd34d';\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(game.star.x, game.star.y, 10 + Math.sin(now / 150) * 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n  }\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  for (const p of game.players) {\n    if (p.gone) continue;\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = '14px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(`${p.name} ${p.score}`, p.x, p.y - R - 8);\n  }\n  ctx.font = '22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n    ctx.font = 'bold 96px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);\n  } else if (game.phase !== 'playing') {\n    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,.55)'; ctx.fillRect(0, H / 2 - 120, W, 240);\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(game.message, W / 2, H / 2 - 70);\n    const rows = game.standings\n      ? game.standings.flatMap((ids, place) => ids.map((id) => [place + 1, game.players.find((p) => p.id === id)]))\n      : game.players.map((p) => [null, p]);\n    ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n    rows.slice(0, 4).forEach(([place, p], i) => {\n      if (!p) return;\n      ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n      ctx.fillText(`${place ? place + '. ' : ''}${p.name}${hub && p.id === hub.me ? ' (you)' : ''} — ${p.score}`, W / 2, H / 2 - 30 + i * 28);\n    });\n  }\n  if (menu.open) drawMenu();\n}\nfunction drawMenu() {\n  ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(10,8,20,.82)'; ctx.fillRect(W / 2 - 170, 150, 340, 70 + menu.items.length * 40);\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = 'bold 22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillText('Settings', W / 2, 186);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ej64h5RaHU6YCybCSZ2tvy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
