{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WfzPXnetdyRTPm8JhTGb7","type":"tool_result","content":"221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n224:- `view.depth(x, y, z = 0)`: true camera depth: use it to sort parts inside one object\n225:- `view.order(x, y, z = 0)`: painter's order for whole objects standing on the ground\n226:- `view.p(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> projected screen pixels (not yet camera-relative)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n228:- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n229:- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n230:- `view.ax`, `view.ay`: screen x = ax * x + ay * y (the projection's first row)\n231:- `view.bx`, `view.by`, `view.bz`: screen y = bx * x + by * y + bz * z (the second row; bz < 0 lifts things up the screen)\n232:- `view.dx`, `view.dy`, `view.dz`: the direction toward the camera, for true depth (view.depth)\n233:- `view.fx`, `view.fy`: the ground direction that points at the camera (the front of a wall faces it)\n234:- `view.id`: its name ('iso', or yours)\n235:- `view.inv`: the inverse of the ground projection (screen -> ground at z 0), null in side views\n236:- `view.isSide`: a side view (pitch 1 or less: x right, z up, y is depth)\n237:- `view.isTop`: looking straight down (pitch 89 or more)\n238:- `view.label`: its name for people ('Isometric')\n239:- `view.pitch`, `view.yaw`: the same angles in radians\n240:- `view.pitchDeg`: the tilt, 0 side view to 90 straight down\n241:- `view.scale`: screen pixels per world unit\n242:- `view.yawDeg`: the turn about the up axis, degrees (0: north is up the screen; iso is 45)\n243:- `view.zBoost`: how much heights are stretched on screen (1 = true)\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n557:- `game.yaw = 0` †: its turn in degrees on top of the view (rotateView)\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968","uuid":"92e1caec-a51f-4ee3-88ef-61262d32290e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:04:38.219Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n224:- `view.depth(x, y, z = 0)`: true camera depth: use it to sort parts inside one object\n225:- `view.order(x, y, z = 0)`: painter's order for whole objects standing on the ground\n226:- `view.p(x, y, z = 0)`: world -> projected screen pixels (not yet camera-relative)\n227:- `view.screenDirToGround(dx, dy)`: a direction the player pushed on screen (x right, y down) -> normalized ground direction\n228:- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n229:- `view.toGround(sx, sy)`: projected screen point -> ground point (z = 0). null in side view\n230:- `view.ax`, `view.ay`: screen x = ax * x + ay * y (the projection's first row)\n231:- `view.bx`, `view.by`, `view.bz`: screen y = bx * x + by * y + bz * z (the second row; bz < 0 lifts things up the screen)\n232:- `view.dx`, `view.dy`, `view.dz`: the direction toward the camera, for true depth (view.depth)\n233:- `view.fx`, `view.fy`: the ground direction that points at the camera (the front of a wall faces it)\n234:- `view.id`: its name ('iso', or yours)\n235:- `view.inv`: the inverse of the ground projection (screen -> ground at z 0), null in side views\n236:- `view.isSide`: a side view (pitch 1 or less: x right, z up, y is depth)\n237:- `view.isTop`: looking straight down (pitch 89 or more)\n238:- `view.label`: its name for people ('Isometric')\n239:- `view.pitch`, `view.yaw`: the same angles in radians\n240:- `view.pitchDeg`: the tilt, 0 side view to 90 straight down\n241:- `view.scale`: screen pixels per world unit\n242:- `view.yawDeg`: the turn about the up axis, degrees (0: north is up the screen; iso is 45)\n243:- `view.zBoost`: how much heights are stretched on screen (1 = true)\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n557:- `game.yaw = 0` †: its turn in degrees on top of the view (rotateView)\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018WfzPXnetdyRTPm8JhTGb7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
