{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014q7rJASeLQm5uj7oWaLTb3","type":"tool_result","content":"276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ...\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n645:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n646:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n650:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n660:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n662:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n700:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968","uuid":"c9525f4a-be99-4dc8-b0b3-8274b85016ed","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:04:48.599Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ...\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n645:- `slash.start(canCancel = false)`: begin a swing if idle (or when canCancel and already recovering). Returns true if it started\n646:- `slash.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n650:- `slash.phase = null`: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', or null when idle\n660:- `combo.state`: what Humanoid.update wants as `attack` (null when idle)\n662:- `combo.idle = 99`: seconds since the last hit ended\n700:- `rig.t`: seconds of its own clock (idle breathing, blinks)\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014q7rJASeLQm5uj7oWaLTb3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
