{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3UusSdRPPTjyV1qq2G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NLvtMeNnUqZ7aCjVqSWUrb","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/work/PLAN.md","offset":480,"limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1278,"cache_read_input_tokens":532578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1278},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968","uuid":"6ab48077-9be2-408f-8006-547adbc41b58","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:18.022Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3UubKukBEFLRZmkP4Q","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NLvtMeNnUqZ7aCjVqSWUrb":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/work/PLAN.md","offset":480,"limit":60}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NLvtMeNnUqZ7aCjVqSWUrb","type":"tool_result","content":"480\t\n481\t### 6.6 Turnovers and possession changes\n482\t- **Interception:** the defender has the ball live and can return it. Control flips (§9.4).\n483\t- **Fumble:** the ball goes loose (§7.7). Whoever recovers has possession. A recovery by the defense is live (can be\n484\t  returned). A recovery by the offense is live too (arcade).\n485\t- **Lateral or backward pass:** legal any time. A bad lateral that hits the ground is a loose ball (a fumble).\n486\t- **Turnover on downs:** the other side takes the ball at the spot.\n487\t- After a change of possession, the line of scrimmage, `dir` and the down reset for the new offense.\n488\t\n489\t---\n490\t\n491\t## 7. Athletes, movement and actions\n492\t\n493\t### 7.1 Ratings\n494\tEach athlete has ratings 1–10: `SPD` speed, `ACC` acceleration and agility (cuts, spins), `STR` strength (blocking,\n495\tbreaking tackles), `HND` hands (catching, ball security), `TCK` tackling, `ARM` throw power, `AIM` throw accuracy,\n496\t`AWR` awareness (AI reaction and reads), `KCK` kicking (power and steadiness). Team ratings on the team-select screen\n497\tare 4 bars averaged from the roster: PASS, RUN, DEFENSE, SPECIAL.\n498\t\n499\t### 7.2 Movement\n500\t- Top speed in units/s = `T.speedBase` (92) + SPD × `T.speedPerSpd` (7), so SPD 2 is 106 (about 6.6 yd/s, a lineman)\n501\t  and SPD 10 is 162 (10.1 yd/s, Zap Zapata).\n502\t- Carrying the ball costs −4%. Backpedaling (moving against `facing` by more than 100°) costs −35%.\n503\t- Acceleration = `T.accelBase` (520) + ACC × 30 units/s². Braking is 900. Turn rate is 9 rad/s at speed and 16 rad/s\n504\t  slow (`E.approachAng`).\n505\t- **Turbo** (b turbo, held): × `T.turboMult` (1.25) speed and × 1.3 acceleration. It drains `T.turboDrain`\n506\t  (0.45/s of a full bar) and regenerates `T.turboRegen` (0.22/s) when not held. Each dead ball refills +35%.\n507\t  Big Hits need turbo ≥ 0.15 and cost 0.15. Every athlete has a bar; the HUD shows the bars of human-held athletes.\n508\t- Surfaces: `mud` × 0.85 speed and × 0.7 acceleration, dives slide 1.5× farther. `ice` × 0.7 grip: velocity\n509\t  approaches the desired one at half the rate (slides), and cuts are wider. Snow weather × 0.95 speed. These come from\n510\t  the floor tag under the athlete (`map.floorAt`).\n511\t- Bodies are `E.Body` (r 6; linemen r 7.5; gravity 700) with `body.update(dt, map)` for z, jumps and the stands.\n512\t  The sim sets `vx, vy` from intents each step.\n513\t\n514\t### 7.3 Collisions between athletes\n515\t- Circle against circle every step for every pair (91 pairs at 14 athletes; no hash needed). Separate along the\n516\t  normal in proportion to the inverse of mass (mass = 1 + STR × 0.15; linemen get +0.6).\n517\t- Teammates push gently. Opponents push hard: no overlap.\n518\t- An overlap with the ball carrier during LIVE is a **contact** and may start a tackle (§7.5). An overlap between a\n519\t  blocker and a rusher starts an **engagement** (§7.9).\n520\t- Refs and sideline cast don't collide with the sim. Refs are pushed aside cosmetically and fall comically if a play\n521\t  runs through them (§10.8).\n522\t\n523\t### 7.4 The action system\n524\tEach athlete has at most one action at a time: `{ id, t, dur, phase, data }`. Actions lock movement as their table\n525\tsays, set the athlete's **pose code** (Appendix C) for the presentation, and resolve at their key moment.\n526\t\n527\t| Action | Who | Input | Duration | Key moment and effect |\n528\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n529\t| `hike` | C | the offense's b1 in PRESNAP | 0.25 s | the ball to the QB (shotgun: an arc in 0.3 s; under center: in hand) |\n530\t| `handoff` | QB → RB | automatic on run plays at the play's `handoffT` | 0.35 s | the ball changes hands when within 1.2 yd; a pitch or toss is a short arc |\n531\t| `throw` | QB | a receiver button, or a click on a receiver | 0.28 s wind + release | the ball's flight (§7.6); with turbo held, a Rocket Pass |\n532\t| `dive` | carrier | b1 | 0.45 s air + 0.6 s down | a lunge of 2.5 yd at 1.4× speed; the ball spot is where he lands; the play ends (down) unless he's in the end zone, which is a TD |\n533\t| `spin` | carrier | b3 | 0.32 s | evade window 0.0–0.22 s: a contact from a tackler that isn't behind him (angle > 110° from his facing) misses; speed × 0.8 during the spin; cooldown 0.8 s |\n534\t| `stiffArm` | carrier | b2 | 0.4 s | a tackler in front (within 60° of facing, within 1.8 yd) gets the break chance + `T.stiffBonus` (0.35); on a break the tackler stumbles (0.6 s down) |\n535\t| `hurdle` | carrier | b4 | 0.55 s (`body.jump(260)`) | airborne: low dives (`dive`, `tackleDive`) pass under him; a standing tackler isn't evaded |\n536\t| `lateral` | carrier | lb or rb | 0.25 s | pitch to the nearest teammate behind or beside him (within 100° of the backward direction, ≤ 9 yd), a 0.35–0.6 s arc; a bad lateral (no teammate in range) is thrown to the nearest spot and is a loose ball |\n537\t| `tackleDive` | defender | b1 (the AI decides when, §8.4) | 0.45 s lunge + 0.7 s down on a miss | contact with the carrier during the lunge resolves a tackle (§7.5) |\n538\t| `bigHit` | defender | turbo + b1 | 0.35 s lunge at 1.6× speed | as a tackle with `T.bigHitBonus` (+0.12) and a fumble roll × 3; a miss is 1.0 s down |\n539\t| `strip` | defender | b3 | 0.3 s | within 1.2 yd of the carrier: fumble chance `T.stripChance` (0.12) − HND × 0.01; otherwise a whiff |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968","uuid":"c37a3ce3-a61f-4551-9d41-35036c8127a8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:18.030Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n### 6.6 Turnovers and possession changes\n- **Interception:** the defender has the ball live and can return it. Control flips (§9.4).\n- **Fumble:** the ball goes loose (§7.7). Whoever recovers has possession. A recovery by the defense is live (can be\n  returned). A recovery by the offense is live too (arcade).\n- **Lateral or backward pass:** legal any time. A bad lateral that hits the ground is a loose ball (a fumble).\n- **Turnover on downs:** the other side takes the ball at the spot.\n- After a change of possession, the line of scrimmage, `dir` and the down reset for the new offense.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Athletes, movement and actions\n\n### 7.1 Ratings\nEach athlete has ratings 1–10: `SPD` speed, `ACC` acceleration and agility (cuts, spins), `STR` strength (blocking,\nbreaking tackles), `HND` hands (catching, ball security), `TCK` tackling, `ARM` throw power, `AIM` throw accuracy,\n`AWR` awareness (AI reaction and reads), `KCK` kicking (power and steadiness). Team ratings on the team-select screen\nare 4 bars averaged from the roster: PASS, RUN, DEFENSE, SPECIAL.\n\n### 7.2 Movement\n- Top speed in units/s = `T.speedBase` (92) + SPD × `T.speedPerSpd` (7), so SPD 2 is 106 (about 6.6 yd/s, a lineman)\n  and SPD 10 is 162 (10.1 yd/s, Zap Zapata).\n- Carrying the ball costs −4%. Backpedaling (moving against `facing` by more than 100°) costs −35%.\n- Acceleration = `T.accelBase` (520) + ACC × 30 units/s². Braking is 900. Turn rate is 9 rad/s at speed and 16 rad/s\n  slow (`E.approachAng`).\n- **Turbo** (b turbo, held): × `T.turboMult` (1.25) speed and × 1.3 acceleration. It drains `T.turboDrain`\n  (0.45/s of a full bar) and regenerates `T.turboRegen` (0.22/s) when not held. Each dead ball refills +35%.\n  Big Hits need turbo ≥ 0.15 and cost 0.15. Every athlete has a bar; the HUD shows the bars of human-held athletes.\n- Surfaces: `mud` × 0.85 speed and × 0.7 acceleration, dives slide 1.5× farther. `ice` × 0.7 grip: velocity\n  approaches the desired one at half the rate (slides), and cuts are wider. Snow weather × 0.95 speed. These come from\n  the floor tag under the athlete (`map.floorAt`).\n- Bodies are `E.Body` (r 6; linemen r 7.5; gravity 700) with `body.update(dt, map)` for z, jumps and the stands.\n  The sim sets `vx, vy` from intents each step.\n\n### 7.3 Collisions between athletes\n- Circle against circle every step for every pair (91 pairs at 14 athletes; no hash needed). Separate along the\n  normal in proportion to the inverse of mass (mass = 1 + STR × 0.15; linemen get +0.6).\n- Teammates push gently. Opponents push hard: no overlap.\n- An overlap with the ball carrier during LIVE is a **contact** and may start a tackle (§7.5). An overlap between a\n  blocker and a rusher starts an **engagement** (§7.9).\n- Refs and sideline cast don't collide with the sim. Refs are pushed aside cosmetically and fall comically if a play\n  runs through them (§10.8).\n\n### 7.4 The action system\nEach athlete has at most one action at a time: `{ id, t, dur, phase, data }`. Actions lock movement as their table\nsays, set the athlete's **pose code** (Appendix C) for the presentation, and resolve at their key moment.\n\n| Action | Who | Input | Duration | Key moment and effect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `hike` | C | the offense's b1 in PRESNAP | 0.25 s | the ball to the QB (shotgun: an arc in 0.3 s; under center: in hand) |\n| `handoff` | QB → RB | automatic on run plays at the play's `handoffT` | 0.35 s | the ball changes hands when within 1.2 yd; a pitch or toss is a short arc |\n| `throw` | QB | a receiver button, or a click on a receiver | 0.28 s wind + release | the ball's flight (§7.6); with turbo held, a Rocket Pass |\n| `dive` | carrier | b1 | 0.45 s air + 0.6 s down | a lunge of 2.5 yd at 1.4× speed; the ball spot is where he lands; the play ends (down) unless he's in the end zone, which is a TD |\n| `spin` | carrier | b3 | 0.32 s | evade window 0.0–0.22 s: a contact from a tackler that isn't behind him (angle > 110° from his facing) misses; speed × 0.8 during the spin; cooldown 0.8 s |\n| `stiffArm` | carrier | b2 | 0.4 s | a tackler in front (within 60° of facing, within 1.8 yd) gets the break chance + `T.stiffBonus` (0.35); on a break the tackler stumbles (0.6 s down) |\n| `hurdle` | carrier | b4 | 0.55 s (`body.jump(260)`) | airborne: low dives (`dive`, `tackleDive`) pass under him; a standing tackler isn't evaded |\n| `lateral` | carrier | lb or rb | 0.25 s | pitch to the nearest teammate behind or beside him (within 100° of the backward direction, ≤ 9 yd), a 0.35–0.6 s arc; a bad lateral (no teammate in range) is thrown to the nearest spot and is a loose ball |\n| `tackleDive` | defender | b1 (the AI decides when, §8.4) | 0.45 s lunge + 0.7 s down on a miss | contact with the carrier during the lunge resolves a tackle (§7.5) |\n| `bigHit` | defender | turbo + b1 | 0.35 s lunge at 1.6× speed | as a tackle with `T.bigHitBonus` (+0.12) and a fumble roll × 3; a miss is 1.0 s down |\n| `strip` | defender | b3 | 0.3 s | within 1.2 yd of the carrier: fumble chance `T.stripChance` (0.12) − HND × 0.01; otherwise a whiff |","numLines":60,"startLine":480,"totalLines":2454}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NLvtMeNnUqZ7aCjVqSWUrb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
