{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q1BffuS4TkK2Bj9JuZ3chW","type":"tool_result","content":"870\t- **Turnovers:** at an INT or a fumble recovery, the humans of the side that gained the ball take the carrier (the\n871\t  first human) and the nearest teammates. The other side's humans take their nearest defenders.\n872\t- **Kicks:** the kicking human runs the meter. The receiving human controls the returner.\n873\t- **Hub sessions:** the same rules, keyed by seat (§16.4).\n874\t- A ring under each held athlete in the player's color (local: `E.PLAYER_COLORS`; sessions: the seat color), and a\n875\t  tag over him (\"P1\", or the hub name) during PRESNAP and for 1 s after each switch.\n876\t\n877\t### 9.5 The mouse on the field\n878\t- Every athlete is drawn with `r.actor(..., { pick: athleteId })`. Each step, `r.pick(...input.pointer())` gives the\n879\t  hovered athlete. Hovering a receiver while QB highlights his chip, and a left click (`input.clicked()`) throws to\n880\t  him (Shift held: a Rocket Pass). Hovering a defender on defense outlines him, and a click switches to him.\n881\t- Pre-snap on offense, a click on the QB or the ball hikes.\n882\t- During the kick meter, a click anywhere presses it.\n883\t- Clicking open ground does nothing in play. A click is never bound to b1, which avoids accidental hikes and dives.\n884\t- The pointer hides after 2 s without mouse movement. `input.lastDevice` switches back to the keyboard on the next\n885\t  key.\n886\t\n887\t---\n888\t\n889\t## 10. The over-the-top systems (`36-ots.js`)\n890\t\n891\t### 10.1 Hot Streak (\"BLAZING!\")\n892\t- **Big plays** are: a TD, a catch of 20+ yd, a run of 15+ yd, a sack, an INT, a forced fumble, and a Big Hit that\n893\t  tackles. Each athlete keeps a heat count. +1 per big play by him. It resets when the opponents make a big play\n894\t  against him (a sack of that QB, a tackle for a loss on that carrier, a pick of that QB) or when they score.\n895\t- At heat 3 he goes **BLAZING** for `T.hotPlays` (6 plays), or until a reset event happens:\n896\t  - unlimited turbo, +12% speed;\n897\t  - offense: tackle p −0.15 against him;\n898\t  - defense: tackle p +0.15, Big Hit fumble ×2;\n899\t  - a QB: aim error ×0.6 and fire-trail passes;\n900\t  - visuals: fire particles at his feet and shoulders (`particles.fire` every 0.05 s, emissive), a flaming ball while\n901\t    he has it, an orange light on him at night;\n902\t  - audio: the music's `hot` layer comes in (`audio.layer('hot', 1, .5)`), the crowd chants, the announcer's\n903\t    `hotStreakOn` lines.\n904\t- A team can have 2 blazing athletes. The HUD shows a flame icon by his name and a heat pip count (1–3) on held\n905\t  athletes' tags.\n906\t\n907\t### 10.2 The Fiasco Meter and the Fiasco Cards (the items)\n908\t**The Fiasco Meter** is the title's mechanic: every disaster is an opportunity. Each team's meter (0–100) fills when\n909\tthings go wrong for it:\n910\t\n911\t| Event | Fill |\n912\t|---|---|\n913\t| fumble lost | 35 |\n914\t| INT thrown | 35 |\n915\t| safety allowed | 40 |\n916\t| sacked | 20 |\n917\t| turnover on downs | 25 |\n918\t| opponent's TD | 20 |\n919\t| dropped pass | 10 |\n920\t| Big Hit received | 10 |\n921\t| late hit received | 5 |\n922\t\n923\tWhen it fills, the team **draws a Fiasco Card** at random from its pool (story: the cards you've unlocked;\n924\texhibition: all 8), up to 3 held. Then the meter resets. A HUD flourish plays: a card flips in, \"FIASCO BREAK!\".\n925\tEach team also starts a game with cards: story, a loadout of up to 3 picked on the chapter screen; exhibition, 1\n926\trandom card each; hub rounds, 1 each, dealt from `AIHub.rng('cards')`.\n927\t\n928\t**Using a card:** on the play-call screen press b4 (△) to open the card row and pick one (or click a slot). One card\n929\tper play. A card on offense needs an offensive card and so on; a card that doesn't fit the side is greyed out. Its\n930\teffect lasts as its text says. Cards are data: `{ id, name, side: 'off' | 'def' | 'any' | 'kick', text, art,\n931\tapply(ctx) }`. `apply` registers bus modifiers for the play or for N plays. The CPU trigger is in §8.5.\n932\t\n933\t| Card | Side | Effect | CPU uses it when |\n934\t|---|---|---|---|\n935\t| ROCKET CLEATS | off | your carrier and receivers +20% speed this play | 3rd & 10+, or trailing in the last 2:00 |\n936\t| GLUE GLOVES | off | your receivers can't drop the ball; contested catches +30% this play | a pass play on 3rd or 4th down |\n937\t| BRICK WALL | off | your blockers can't be shed for 3.5 s | a pass play on 3rd & long |\n938\t| HOT SAUCE | any | the held athlete (CPU: its best player) goes BLAZING for 3 plays | first chance in the 2nd half |\n939\t| MEGA HIT | def | this play's first tackle is a Mega Hit: launch × 1.6, fumble chance 60%, the slow-mo cam | 3rd down defense, or the opponent in the red zone |\n940\t| BUTTERFINGERS | def | opposing receivers' catch chance −35% this play | 3rd & long defense |\n941\t| MASCOT MAYHEM | any | your mascot runs on as a 12th player for the play: he blocks the nearest defender on offense, rushes the passer on defense, with `noClip` through blockers. The announcers lose their minds. | trailing by 7+ |\n942\t| SUPER FOOT | kick | the next kick: +15 yd, an accuracy band ×2.5, the power needle ×0.7 speed | a FG of 45+ yd, or a PAT in the last minute |\n943\t\n944\t### 10.3 Big Hits, Mega Hits, Dinged and the flying helmet\n945\t- **Big Hit:** turbo + b1 (§7.4–7.5). Hit-stop 0.08 s, `game.shake(4)`, `game.hitFx` with an impact star, grass, mud\n946\t  or snow bits, a camera punch-in to 1.25× for 0.35 s, slow motion (`timeScale` 0.4 for 0.3 s, honoring reduce\n947\t  motion), a comic \"BOOM!\" / \"WHAM!\" / \"KER-RUNCH!\" burst over the hit, and the crowd \"OOOOH\".\n948\t- **Mega Hit** (the card, or a 1-in-6 roll of a Blazing Big Hit): launch × 1.6, the victim spins in the air (PoseFX\n949\t  spin), hit-stop 0.12, the slow-mo cam (`timeScale` 0.25 for 0.6 s), a white flash (`game.flash`, honoring the\n950\t  flashes setting).\n951\t- **Dinged:** the victim of a Mega Hit, or of 2 Big Hits in one drive, is Dinged for 2 plays: −10% speed and little\n952\t  cartoon stars orbiting his helmet (3 tiny glints circling, emissive).\n953\t- **The flying helmet:** on a Mega Hit (and 25% of Big Hits) the victim's helmet pops off as a separate bouncing\n954\t  prop: a shape `helmet` in team colors, an `E.Body` with bounce 0.5. His hair shows until the next PRESNAP, when he\n955\t  picks it up (cosmetic). The announcer says \"HIS HELMET IS IN A DIFFERENT AREA CODE!\"\n956\t\n957\t### 10.4 Late hits\n958\tAfter the whistle, for 1.2 s, b1 near an opponent does a late hit (cosmetic knockdown). The refs throw their caps\n959\t(Fiasco rules: no flags). A crowd reaction, the announcer's outrage lines, a stat. AI athletes late-hit too, by team\n960\tpersonality (the Mudhogs often, the Dynasty sneakily).\n961\t\n962\t### 10.5 Boss specials (story bosses; also in exhibition)\n963\tEach special is used by the AI, or by a human holding that star (b4 pressed together with b1 when the conditions\n964\thold). A badge shows \"SPECIAL READY\" on the star's tag.\n965\t\n966\t| Star | Special | Rules |\n967\t|---|---|---|\n968\t| BIG BERTHA BOUDREAUX (Mudhogs RB #44) | **MUDSLIDE** | once per drive: for 1.2 s she lowers her shoulder; the first tackler in front is bowled over (down 1.2 s) unless it's a Big Hit from the front; mud spray FX |\n969\t| LUMEN LOPEZ (Owls QB #1) | **NIGHT VISION** | always on: his reads see 1 extra yard of openness, and his aim error ×0.8 |\n970\t| ZAP ZAPATA (Owls WR #11) | **AFTERBURNER** | once per play: a 1.0 s burst at ×1.35 speed that leaves neon light trails (`ghost` afterimages in cyan) |\n971\t| AVALANCHE (Yetis DE #99) | **SNOWPLOW** | once per drive: his engagement drives the blocker straight back at 3× push for 1.5 s; a snow spray |\n972\t| BROCK STERLING III (Dynasty QB #12) | **GOLDEN SPIRAL** | once per drive: a perfect pass, no aim error, it can't be intercepted (defenders may still deflect it with 0.15), gold sparkle trail |\n973\t| THE MOUNTAIN, MALU FALEOLO (Dynasty LB #55) | **SEISMIC SACK** | once per half, when within 3 yd of the carrier: he leaps (0.6 s) and slams down; everyone within 2.5 yd is knocked down; a shockwave ring (`particles.ring`), shake 7, \"SEISMIC!\" |\n974\tThe commentary has lines for each, and the HUD shows a banner with the star's portrait for 1.2 s when one fires.\n975\t\n976\t### 10.6 Celebrations\n977\tAfter a TD the scorer celebrates. Locally the scorer's human picks one: b2 the Charleston, b3 the Body Roll, b4 the\n978\tHelicopter (breakdance). Otherwise it's random by personality, from the list below. In hub sessions it's always\n979\trandom (no player-triggered emotes, §16.7).\n980\t\n981\t| Celebration | How it's animated |\n982\t|---|---|\n983\t| Spike | a throw-down attack spec, the ball bounces high |\n984\t| Charleston, Body Roll | mocap `Dance Charleston` / `Dance Body Roll` |\n985\t| Helicopter | mocap `Breakdance_Helicopter` |\n986\t| Backflip | mocap `Backflip` |\n987\t| Fist pump | mocap `Victory Fist Pump` |\n988\t| Stands Dive | he leaps into the end zone stands: `body.jump`, the crowd lifts him, bodies bob |\n989\t| Group Huddle Dance | 3 nearest teammates do `Dance_Loop` in a ring |\n990\t\n991\tTeammates near him do `Cheering_Two_Hands`. Defenders kneel (`pose: 'kneel'`) or put their hands on their helmets\n992\t(PoseFX). Pyro cannons fire, confetti falls (`particles.bits` in team colors from z 160), the crowd goes wild.\n993\t\n994\t### 10.7 Mascots\n995\tEach team has a mascot on the near sideline: a Humanoid in team colors with a big costume head drawn by the gear\n996\thook (§12.2). They react: dance on scores, slump on turnovers, and do a backflip on a Big Hit. They flip the coin, and\n997\trun on with Mascot Mayhem (`noClip`, a cartoon dust cloud, a squeaky sfx). Fumbles the Flaming Tumbleweed sets\n998\thimself on fire when the Fiascos score (fire particles), and trips over the power cable in chapter 3 (§15.1).\n999\t\n1000\t### 10.8 Refs\n1001\tTwo refs on the field (an umpire 6 yd behind the defense, a back judge 20 yd deep) and a line judge on the near\n1002\tsideline. They're cosmetic Humanoids in striped shirts (the gear hook draws the stripes), with poses for signals:\n1003\tTOUCHDOWN (both arms up), FIRST DOWN (an arm pointing at the offense's goal), INCOMPLETE (arms crossing, a wave),\n1004\tFUMBLE / POSSESSION (pointing), and \"Sure, why not\" (a shrug) after a late hit. A play running through a ref knocks"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c28e7abf-db6e-401a-a911-43ba9983a968","uuid":"810fb085-bddb-4f30-ac3a-06b74dde562b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:51:02.955Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174831__x898ed5/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Turnovers:** at an INT or a fumble recovery, the humans of the side that gained the ball take the carrier (the\n  first human) and the nearest teammates. The other side's humans take their nearest defenders.\n- **Kicks:** the kicking human runs the meter. The receiving human controls the returner.\n- **Hub sessions:** the same rules, keyed by seat (§16.4).\n- A ring under each held athlete in the player's color (local: `E.PLAYER_COLORS`; sessions: the seat color), and a\n  tag over him (\"P1\", or the hub name) during PRESNAP and for 1 s after each switch.\n\n### 9.5 The mouse on the field\n- Every athlete is drawn with `r.actor(..., { pick: athleteId })`. Each step, `r.pick(...input.pointer())` gives the\n  hovered athlete. Hovering a receiver while QB highlights his chip, and a left click (`input.clicked()`) throws to\n  him (Shift held: a Rocket Pass). Hovering a defender on defense outlines him, and a click switches to him.\n- Pre-snap on offense, a click on the QB or the ball hikes.\n- During the kick meter, a click anywhere presses it.\n- Clicking open ground does nothing in play. A click is never bound to b1, which avoids accidental hikes and dives.\n- The pointer hides after 2 s without mouse movement. `input.lastDevice` switches back to the keyboard on the next\n  key.\n\n---\n\n## 10. The over-the-top systems (`36-ots.js`)\n\n### 10.1 Hot Streak (\"BLAZING!\")\n- **Big plays** are: a TD, a catch of 20+ yd, a run of 15+ yd, a sack, an INT, a forced fumble, and a Big Hit that\n  tackles. Each athlete keeps a heat count. +1 per big play by him. It resets when the opponents make a big play\n  against him (a sack of that QB, a tackle for a loss on that carrier, a pick of that QB) or when they score.\n- At heat 3 he goes **BLAZING** for `T.hotPlays` (6 plays), or until a reset event happens:\n  - unlimited turbo, +12% speed;\n  - offense: tackle p −0.15 against him;\n  - defense: tackle p +0.15, Big Hit fumble ×2;\n  - a QB: aim error ×0.6 and fire-trail passes;\n  - visuals: fire particles at his feet and shoulders (`particles.fire` every 0.05 s, emissive), a flaming ball while\n    he has it, an orange light on him at night;\n  - audio: the music's `hot` layer comes in (`audio.layer('hot', 1, .5)`), the crowd chants, the announcer's\n    `hotStreakOn` lines.\n- A team can have 2 blazing athletes. The HUD shows a flame icon by his name and a heat pip count (1–3) on held\n  athletes' tags.\n\n### 10.2 The Fiasco Meter and the Fiasco Cards (the items)\n**The Fiasco Meter** is the title's mechanic: every disaster is an opportunity. Each team's meter (0–100) fills when\nthings go wrong for it:\n\n| Event | Fill |\n|---|---|\n| fumble lost | 35 |\n| INT thrown | 35 |\n| safety allowed | 40 |\n| sacked | 20 |\n| turnover on downs | 25 |\n| opponent's TD | 20 |\n| dropped pass | 10 |\n| Big Hit received | 10 |\n| late hit received | 5 |\n\nWhen it fills, the team **draws a Fiasco Card** at random from its pool (story: the cards you've unlocked;\nexhibition: all 8), up to 3 held. Then the meter resets. A HUD flourish plays: a card flips in, \"FIASCO BREAK!\".\nEach team also starts a game with cards: story, a loadout of up to 3 picked on the chapter screen; exhibition, 1\nrandom card each; hub rounds, 1 each, dealt from `AIHub.rng('cards')`.\n\n**Using a card:** on the play-call screen press b4 (△) to open the card row and pick one (or click a slot). One card\nper play. A card on offense needs an offensive card and so on; a card that doesn't fit the side is greyed out. Its\neffect lasts as its text says. Cards are data: `{ id, name, side: 'off' | 'def' | 'any' | 'kick', text, art,\napply(ctx) }`. `apply` registers bus modifiers for the play or for N plays. The CPU trigger is in §8.5.\n\n| Card | Side | Effect | CPU uses it when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ROCKET CLEATS | off | your carrier and receivers +20% speed this play | 3rd & 10+, or trailing in the last 2:00 |\n| GLUE GLOVES | off | your receivers can't drop the ball; contested catches +30% this play | a pass play on 3rd or 4th down |\n| BRICK WALL | off | your blockers can't be shed for 3.5 s | a pass play on 3rd & long |\n| HOT SAUCE | any | the held athlete (CPU: its best player) goes BLAZING for 3 plays | first chance in the 2nd half |\n| MEGA HIT | def | this play's first tackle is a Mega Hit: launch × 1.6, fumble chance 60%, the slow-mo cam | 3rd down defense, or the opponent in the red zone |\n| BUTTERFINGERS | def | opposing receivers' catch chance −35% this play | 3rd & long defense |\n| MASCOT MAYHEM | any | your mascot runs on as a 12th player for the play: he blocks the nearest defender on offense, rushes the passer on defense, with `noClip` through blockers. The announcers lose their minds. | trailing by 7+ |\n| SUPER FOOT | kick | the next kick: +15 yd, an accuracy band ×2.5, the power needle ×0.7 speed | a FG of 45+ yd, or a PAT in the last minute |\n\n### 10.3 Big Hits, Mega Hits, Dinged and the flying helmet\n- **Big Hit:** turbo + b1 (§7.4–7.5). Hit-stop 0.08 s, `game.shake(4)`, `game.hitFx` with an impact star, grass, mud\n  or snow bits, a camera punch-in to 1.25× for 0.35 s, slow motion (`timeScale` 0.4 for 0.3 s, honoring reduce\n  motion), a comic \"BOOM!\" / \"WHAM!\" / \"KER-RUNCH!\" burst over the hit, and the crowd \"OOOOH\".\n- **Mega Hit** (the card, or a 1-in-6 roll of a Blazing Big Hit): launch × 1.6, the victim spins in the air (PoseFX\n  spin), hit-stop 0.12, the slow-mo cam (`timeScale` 0.25 for 0.6 s), a white flash (`game.flash`, honoring the\n  flashes setting).\n- **Dinged:** the victim of a Mega Hit, or of 2 Big Hits in one drive, is Dinged for 2 plays: −10% speed and little\n  cartoon stars orbiting his helmet (3 tiny glints circling, emissive).\n- **The flying helmet:** on a Mega Hit (and 25% of Big Hits) the victim's helmet pops off as a separate bouncing\n  prop: a shape `helmet` in team colors, an `E.Body` with bounce 0.5. His hair shows until the next PRESNAP, when he\n  picks it up (cosmetic). The announcer says \"HIS HELMET IS IN A DIFFERENT AREA CODE!\"\n\n### 10.4 Late hits\nAfter the whistle, for 1.2 s, b1 near an opponent does a late hit (cosmetic knockdown). The refs throw their caps\n(Fiasco rules: no flags). A crowd reaction, the announcer's outrage lines, a stat. AI athletes late-hit too, by team\npersonality (the Mudhogs often, the Dynasty sneakily).\n\n### 10.5 Boss specials (story bosses; also in exhibition)\nEach special is used by the AI, or by a human holding that star (b4 pressed together with b1 when the conditions\nhold). A badge shows \"SPECIAL READY\" on the star's tag.\n\n| Star | Special | Rules |\n|---|---|---|\n| BIG BERTHA BOUDREAUX (Mudhogs RB #44) | **MUDSLIDE** | once per drive: for 1.2 s she lowers her shoulder; the first tackler in front is bowled over (down 1.2 s) unless it's a Big Hit from the front; mud spray FX |\n| LUMEN LOPEZ (Owls QB #1) | **NIGHT VISION** | always on: his reads see 1 extra yard of openness, and his aim error ×0.8 |\n| ZAP ZAPATA (Owls WR #11) | **AFTERBURNER** | once per play: a 1.0 s burst at ×1.35 speed that leaves neon light trails (`ghost` afterimages in cyan) |\n| AVALANCHE (Yetis DE #99) | **SNOWPLOW** | once per drive: his engagement drives the blocker straight back at 3× push for 1.5 s; a snow spray |\n| BROCK STERLING III (Dynasty QB #12) | **GOLDEN SPIRAL** | once per drive: a perfect pass, no aim error, it can't be intercepted (defenders may still deflect it with 0.15), gold sparkle trail |\n| THE MOUNTAIN, MALU FALEOLO (Dynasty LB #55) | **SEISMIC SACK** | once per half, when within 3 yd of the carrier: he leaps (0.6 s) and slams down; everyone within 2.5 yd is knocked down; a shockwave ring (`particles.ring`), shake 7, \"SEISMIC!\" |\nThe commentary has lines for each, and the HUD shows a banner with the star's portrait for 1.2 s when one fires.\n\n### 10.6 Celebrations\nAfter a TD the scorer celebrates. Locally the scorer's human picks one: b2 the Charleston, b3 the Body Roll, b4 the\nHelicopter (breakdance). Otherwise it's random by personality, from the list below. In hub sessions it's always\nrandom (no player-triggered emotes, §16.7).\n\n| Celebration | How it's animated |\n|---|---|\n| Spike | a throw-down attack spec, the ball bounces high |\n| Charleston, Body Roll | mocap `Dance Charleston` / `Dance Body Roll` |\n| Helicopter | mocap `Breakdance_Helicopter` |\n| Backflip | mocap `Backflip` |\n| Fist pump | mocap `Victory Fist Pump` |\n| Stands Dive | he leaps into the end zone stands: `body.jump`, the crowd lifts him, bodies bob |\n| Group Huddle Dance | 3 nearest teammates do `Dance_Loop` in a ring |\n\nTeammates near him do `Cheering_Two_Hands`. Defenders kneel (`pose: 'kneel'`) or put their hands on their helmets\n(PoseFX). Pyro cannons fire, confetti falls (`particles.bits` in team colors from z 160), the crowd goes wild.\n\n### 10.7 Mascots\nEach team has a mascot on the near sideline: a Humanoid in team colors with a big costume head drawn by the gear\nhook (§12.2). They react: dance on scores, slump on turnovers, and do a backflip on a Big Hit. They flip the coin, and\nrun on with Mascot Mayhem (`noClip`, a cartoon dust cloud, a squeaky sfx). Fumbles the Flaming Tumbleweed sets\nhimself on fire when the Fiascos score (fire particles), and trips over the power cable in chapter 3 (§15.1).\n\n### 10.8 Refs\nTwo refs on the field (an umpire 6 yd behind the defense, a back judge 20 yd deep) and a line judge on the near\nsideline. They're cosmetic Humanoids in striped shirts (the gear hook draws the stripes), with poses for signals:\nTOUCHDOWN (both arms up), FIRST DOWN (an arm pointing at the offense's goal), INCOMPLETE (arms crossing, a wave),\nFUMBLE / POSSESSION (pointing), and \"Sure, why not\" (a shrug) after a late hit. A play running through a ref knocks","numLines":135,"startLine":870,"totalLines":2487}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q1BffuS4TkK2Bj9JuZ3chW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
